# Trivy vulnerability suppression file.
#
# When adding a suppression, keep the format:
#   # <package>: <what the CVE is and why the risk is accepted>
#   CVE-XXXX-YYYY exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# Always set an expiry date so the suppression is revisited instead of
# silently outliving the base image it was written for.
# See: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/

# openssl (openssl, libssl3t64, openssl-provider-legacy): DTLS retransmission
# out-of-bounds read; the container speaks TLS over TCP only, no DTLS
CVE-2026-84782 exp:2026-11-01

# openssl (openssl, libssl3t64, openssl-provider-legacy): QUIC stack ignores
# connection-level flow control; no QUIC in the container, nginx terminates TLS
CVE-2026-75804 exp:2026-11-01

# libpcre2-8-0: JIT out-of-bounds write with an attacker-controlled pattern;
# Python's re does not use PCRE2 and no user-supplied regex reaches it
CVE-2026-103111 exp:2026-11-01
